key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160967/selection/3dd226b257fbc245076072ba0b19ce6c90d8564f29c8fdc18895ff04fa69ae73" :answer-field/choices ["q-160967/selection/6904057c137757d909847c7cf0a7ad9b710b7f2fba86224e9fbff6113291b565" "q-160967/selection/554150977856e104e470f4719d8e1db9f8a7ff1aacfba0a826a78b8d988cf749" "q-160967/selection/3dd226b257fbc245076072ba0b19ce6c90d8564f29c8fdc18895ff04fa69ae73" "q-160967/selection/a90aa396b4ff9ec18fff24209b24709477c21a51ae5fc1acd9741500ad836c69" "q-160967/selection/d8973ae1101b1e1062edbcea5570fbf22599ddfff251008f7c695b829af01442"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160967" :question/id #uuid "cef91c5c-6d4e-5d54-a2c1-586a57e9523c" :question/math-academy-id "q-160967" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/21952fe273fd1a1ecb03727f4aa254d4e0ecdab2feaeb1d8c652bc9923404846.png)\n\nConsider the rectangular region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,3\\le u\\le 4,\\,\\,\\frac{13\\pi }{12}\\le v\\le \\frac{13\\pi }{9}},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v).\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the image of the left side of $Δ$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the left side.\n\nFor the left side, we have $u=3$ and $\\frac{13\\pi }{12}\\le v\\le \\frac{13\\pi }{9}.$ \n\nSubstituting $u=3$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{13\\pi }{12}\\le v\\le \\frac{13\\pi }{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is an equation of a circular arc of radius $3$ centered at the origin in the $xy$-plane. \nThe arc lies in the third quadrant between the polar rays $\\theta =\\frac{13\\pi }{12}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{13\\pi }{9},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/3b8b1c7b2a7e68aee7a685e946a0b248470dbe4c5d4dcdfec9cd22783529345c.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-160967/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "992d4af7-bdf3-50ef-b524-bc609271541a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160967"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-160942/selection/64ef1b3cee22c5084421be7b8b86ff1bcafe85ba10f9df7b6d31bd6fc6ce4eb7" :answer/id #uuid "6e4f7035-4638-56bf-b95a-0a8f4a672bf1" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/32aa42ca7dc665fb0a486f9a4f984916857d3964934c7a74c50723f1018fd833.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160942/selection/b4644cf00780c5582595123ae18877058981ef3ab71509ebc07676faef582141" :answer/id #uuid "5aa9471f-2005-56b5-886b-1c8e430ac917" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/49ea0e312d1572a3e598ae1962fac6fd10e61835b40c73310792857eb0dc2380.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160942/selection/673f4222b75e0407ed5be7c4ce9fb570a859be32574d54636e3d2275bd049250" :answer/id #uuid "a54f7e81-557a-58af-bab5-b17a483c6d21" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/9f3fd1164ab4346961dab3ab258cf06ccd7aea62644375feeb2b24690c3ca718.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160942/selection/cf3b9162b9cbbfcef6fea8b7e60f3f0507314ddda5dfaab4c423491d721db554" :answer/id #uuid "7071b572-26fd-547f-b29d-798968e64b30" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/3b09b73c500e5c08dd443f1a53f8fbc1a644d18bcd90aa3e96bc1a02e77db75b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160942/selection/a90aa396b4ff9ec18fff24209b24709477c21a51ae5fc1acd9741500ad836c69" :answer/id #uuid "c008f5f8-c68a-5437-9f84-03a1b21ede2f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The image is the empty set" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160942/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4cc789c-512d-50e8-b212-43c0683563d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160942/selection/64ef1b3cee22c5084421be7b8b86ff1bcafe85ba10f9df7b6d31bd6fc6ce4eb7" :answer-field/choices ["q-160942/selection/64ef1b3cee22c5084421be7b8b86ff1bcafe85ba10f9df7b6d31bd6fc6ce4eb7" "q-160942/selection/b4644cf00780c5582595123ae18877058981ef3ab71509ebc07676faef582141" "q-160942/selection/673f4222b75e0407ed5be7c4ce9fb570a859be32574d54636e3d2275bd049250" "q-160942/selection/cf3b9162b9cbbfcef6fea8b7e60f3f0507314ddda5dfaab4c423491d721db554" "q-160942/selection/a90aa396b4ff9ec18fff24209b24709477c21a51ae5fc1acd9741500ad836c69"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160942" :question/id #uuid "cfb7c239-a64d-500a-8d8c-d627867333a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-160942" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/0412da40e0e04e8da5ec92db1ad665251209a718333ec008ceeebbe308c71855.png)\n\nConsider the rectangular region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v).\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the image of the left side of $Δ$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the left side.\n\nFor the left side, we have $u=0$ and $0\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ \n\nSubstituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(0\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,0\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(0,\\,0),\\,0\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the point $(0,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/32aa42ca7dc665fb0a486f9a4f984916857d3964934c7a74c50723f1018fd833.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-160942/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "992d4af7-bdf3-50ef-b524-bc609271541a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160942"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161031/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "e05fcd1e-0f8f-574f-9c83-47b9a035b47b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161031/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "113ec32c-637b-5295-94e3-24b0e629d7a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161031/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "cea40ff5-125b-55e2-ab20-8e0c07318226" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161031/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d53e305f-4453-5bc0-8e90-95ba72600102" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161031/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "c3ebd0ca-4372-55c1-bddd-5f2ada13fa42" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161031/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f060482f-8518-56a6-850c-f026a266ac3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161031/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-161031/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-161031/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-161031/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-161031/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-161031/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161031" :question/id #uuid "bc24e98f-4c39-5479-a484-21b2eaa8a13f" :question/math-academy-id "q-161031" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/0963fc3c56b5baac68e2d587896bf4655950640ecce5b924edc2d8e26a3e64e2.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,\\,0\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v).\n$$\n\nThe image of the bottom side of $Δ$ under the action of $T$ is a line segment. Which of the following statements are true regarding the image?\n\n- The image makes the angle of $0$ with the positive $x$-axis.\n- The image makes the angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ with the positive $x$-axis.\n- One endpoint of the image is the origin $O$ of the $xy$-plane, and the other endpoint lies on the circle of radius $\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $O.$" :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the bottom side.\n\nFor the bottom side, we have $v=0$ and $0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{3}.$ \n\nSubstituting $v=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =(u,\\,0),\\,0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a parametric equation of the line segment shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/92bd315a07a5d76e77c249c12ea4544ee1555b0c214c68cf1f92fc3f07a71ddf.png)\n\n \n\nNote that the line that this segment lies on passes through the origin. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. The slope of the line is\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡0}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, our line makes an angle of $0$ radians with the positive $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement III is true.\n\n- When $u=0,$ we obtain the point \n$(0,\\,0),$\nwhich is the origin $O$ of the $xy$-plane.\n\n- When $u=\\sqrt{3},$ we obtain the point \n$(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0),$\nwhose distance to $O$ is $\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nSo, one endpoint of the segment is the origin $O$ of the $xy$-plane, while the other endpoint lies on the circle with radius $\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $O.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161031/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58fbdce5-60b9-5682-a84e-1c8a5077c762"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161031"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161025/selection/37914587cd4f2887e83bf06e867ab40ef0ad48c2586dea3c0fdce2bfa7a706f0" :answer/id #uuid "8c847e93-968e-5ee2-ab48-0db10ea97c40" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/e50d218c70d9f4f5e77a9ef53b5fb2712b6b400450fc2165e7972b06621b9757.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161025/selection/a90aa396b4ff9ec18fff24209b24709477c21a51ae5fc1acd9741500ad836c69" :answer/id #uuid "c04370dd-6a5c-5385-a0cc-00706bd20b36" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The image is the empty set" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161025/selection/72b07042835d1cbe1ba70047b49d54cab5734892b595318af12bf12b2cb9fa77" :answer/id #uuid "1d480341-5bb5-5579-b875-957e826bf886" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/aafdff659d5c73ab37dfe9cf27c8777d03d7731f04dd106c149e6b4bfbc45fb2.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161025/selection/e2d0449c1e78b00de5def0d03b5832313de1b3a208d9b9c2c0486726a5ec72c7" :answer/id #uuid "9f504099-7786-5b56-9fc8-90ea68cb2d31" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/399dc3c9750ed7e041f1973cad0a24a18903360ba68f0dbcb42c566436c9e259.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161025/selection/5ed7d7fe7dafb22410d0106477506de051227eeb86dab3303c8153ddfe8c896c" :answer/id #uuid "7d7e3ad4-bb40-5baa-97de-71a64ce1a53b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/ee80e889e142c56b48a884a71dd714349ffbb95a6bdee3a3406679ed1edfaaa3.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161025/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "417b0651-eb91-5de7-af46-d6ede2243243" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161025/selection/5ed7d7fe7dafb22410d0106477506de051227eeb86dab3303c8153ddfe8c896c" :answer-field/choices ["q-161025/selection/37914587cd4f2887e83bf06e867ab40ef0ad48c2586dea3c0fdce2bfa7a706f0" "q-161025/selection/a90aa396b4ff9ec18fff24209b24709477c21a51ae5fc1acd9741500ad836c69" "q-161025/selection/72b07042835d1cbe1ba70047b49d54cab5734892b595318af12bf12b2cb9fa77" "q-161025/selection/e2d0449c1e78b00de5def0d03b5832313de1b3a208d9b9c2c0486726a5ec72c7" "q-161025/selection/5ed7d7fe7dafb22410d0106477506de051227eeb86dab3303c8153ddfe8c896c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161025" :question/id #uuid "f7dffa96-ac1f-5c9d-b16b-8ea8f986a8f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-161025" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/de9f7a32a41bcecc1707b90d6818d58473473a4dc26d17e39e957461de95d671.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{6},\\,\\,0\\le v\\le \\frac{5\\pi }{12}},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v).\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the image of the top side of $Δ$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the top side.\n\nFor the top side, we have $v=\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$ and $0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{6}.$ \n\nSubstituting $v=\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{12}),\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{12})),\\,0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a parametric equation of the line segment that makes an angle of $\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$ with the positive $x$-axis, where one endpoint is the point $O,$ while the other endpoint lies on the circle of radius $\\sqrt{6}$ centered at $O,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/ee80e889e142c56b48a884a71dd714349ffbb95a6bdee3a3406679ed1edfaaa3.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161025/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58fbdce5-60b9-5682-a84e-1c8a5077c762"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161025"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161028/selection/7212a94db82d7b9778e2bb61ad40ec0d291bbd0968d1cfa5f265c3efbf8c5b60" :answer/id #uuid "f18cda0c-0738-5cfa-856e-ddcfa6a9ce4e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/48eb6a022826e8f4e1246201e4ad190fff9bb6afdf7b2146d89010e76478a4bf.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161028/selection/29b0ba3c79c0bfc50a0f11a24a66fcc07c99196ecf8c99f265e3b2212e9a6699" :answer/id #uuid "075f3eb3-3f6b-5eb0-8457-44213eb29188" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/a63ab6b0cb9e525901e8173ae54afb89530ae96342975731b76e51b2a51d752e.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161028/selection/19f5e2596c88118080a32542fa888cfe692cb5750bbc9194d58067f92e175609" :answer/id #uuid "ed8cc6a3-b85b-5811-9483-f7eac8fd76f8" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/2d95ce1c0b844b49000b05ef44ef0da8b516740804a8e6bd275a1f9ca15b2ed0.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161028/selection/a90aa396b4ff9ec18fff24209b24709477c21a51ae5fc1acd9741500ad836c69" :answer/id #uuid "436a9d83-28be-54fd-b142-8521492c4290" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The image is the empty set" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161028/selection/5968899f0d34b10849852209884181f2ceec34dd3b0b50546fd9e4059c9fb2c1" :answer/id #uuid "31f13522-703d-5347-90a4-ac4c31e3ccf6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/539932b6d0bc70809848bf1690df34dc56ebb569dc4877c231bd08e8698c5764.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161028/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3faa8fe0-2805-5f5c-a1c0-59317f76260b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161028/selection/7212a94db82d7b9778e2bb61ad40ec0d291bbd0968d1cfa5f265c3efbf8c5b60" :answer-field/choices ["q-161028/selection/7212a94db82d7b9778e2bb61ad40ec0d291bbd0968d1cfa5f265c3efbf8c5b60" "q-161028/selection/29b0ba3c79c0bfc50a0f11a24a66fcc07c99196ecf8c99f265e3b2212e9a6699" "q-161028/selection/19f5e2596c88118080a32542fa888cfe692cb5750bbc9194d58067f92e175609" "q-161028/selection/a90aa396b4ff9ec18fff24209b24709477c21a51ae5fc1acd9741500ad836c69" "q-161028/selection/5968899f0d34b10849852209884181f2ceec34dd3b0b50546fd9e4059c9fb2c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161028" :question/id #uuid "28df611d-b4f1-50bf-9ab3-8cd1c3286161" :question/math-academy-id "q-161028" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/aa62dda1abb7bc6bca1b2e6cdf356b52946820912ec6318e5901273a546ee96a.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 4,\\,\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\le v\\le \\frac{7\\pi }{6}},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v).\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the image of the bottom side of $Δ$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the bottom side.\n\nFor the bottom side, we have $v=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ and $0\\le u\\le 4.$ \n\nSubstituting $v=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}),\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})),\\,0\\le u\\le 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a parametric equation of the line segment that makes an angle of $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ with the positive $x$-axis, where one endpoint is the point $O,$ while the other endpoint lies on the circle of radius $4$ centered at $O,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/48eb6a022826e8f4e1246201e4ad190fff9bb6afdf7b2146d89010e76478a4bf.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161028/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58fbdce5-60b9-5682-a84e-1c8a5077c762"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161028"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161035/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d955ac6a-3174-55aa-97c9-6fa15e14011c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161035/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "b6bab996-f996-5847-8234-1d847b915573" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161035/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "516d43a6-002e-5ed9-aecc-54f9a0fd2a05" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161035/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" :answer/id #uuid "dfe8265c-558c-56f5-a30a-15de3b13cd40" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161035/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "27684675-c376-5bb0-99aa-74fbecda7e2b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161035/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "28392b5c-1b32-5346-bbc0-aebc06dc938a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-161035/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-161035/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-161035/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-161035/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-161035/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" "q-161035/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-161035" :question/id #uuid "ff953a39-6efa-54c4-a86e-77d5c7de4aa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161035" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/8afe0884ccf1e62ffdfef6cab4626bc59b3138aa5cd26f855980c88971753447.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{5},\\,\\,0\\le v\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{4}},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v).\n$$\n\nThe image of the top side of $Δ$ under the action of $T$ is a line segment. Which of the following statements are true regarding the image?\n\n- The image makes the angle of $0$ with the positive $x$-axis.\n- The image makes the angle of $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ with the positive $x$-axis.\n- One endpoint of the image is the origin $O$ of the $xy$-plane, and the other endpoint lies on the circle of radius $5$ centered at $O.$" :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the top side.\n\nFor the top side, we have $v=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ and $0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{5}.$ \n\nSubstituting $v=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}),\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})),\\,0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a parametric equation of the line segment shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/b836799bc512db70d2ce5fcfe70db2af3b2572d584d317fa5ed515b363a11ddc.png)\n\n \n\nNote that the line that this segment lies on passes through the origin. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. The slope of the line is\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nAs a result, our line makes an angle of $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ radians with the positive $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement III is false.\n\n- When $u=0,$ we obtain the point $(0,\\,0),$ which is the origin $O$ of the $xy$-plane.\n\n- When $u=\\sqrt{5},$ we obtain the point \n$(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}),\\,\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})),$\nwhose distance to $O$ is $\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nSo, one endpoint of the segment is the origin $O$ of the $xy$-plane, while the other endpoint lies in the circle with radius $\\sqrt{5}$ centered at $O.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161035/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58fbdce5-60b9-5682-a84e-1c8a5077c762"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-161035"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161026/selection/77808cf54ac3aad0e531702354c8129f40666bdc0a21dd6e7afe05db2e308a5d" :answer/id #uuid "72ce25d4-ed17-55ec-ab3c-d89f301eaab7" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/d329b641155ad693c515ed4d8229f8bd7dbd9d0aab8442e9f65391316d5aa7a3.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161026/selection/b5cb5f60a239b0127a0db3134c0d3c8835753bdb1ef06756698ea9ad2ead6b4d" :answer/id #uuid "76249444-4841-59c7-bcf6-835606a28450" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/cbcba98cd11ce740be941848d0d9d4524c8cbc58d6de7aee0cfb2f7421c457db.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161026/selection/a90aa396b4ff9ec18fff24209b24709477c21a51ae5fc1acd9741500ad836c69" :answer/id #uuid "be8102ce-d018-5bee-a57e-7fcfb32c8a63" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The image is the empty set" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161026/selection/c6c89d18f8bfd3c53eca9815eb55bcfa56f7cc25f6551e1f40cc3f4af1ce9d36" :answer/id #uuid "94cd4ae7-2fb7-561a-abcd-0e59c3eee05d" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/deafbae15e6d30f175122d3662397f05398d31579b80520648accaf1fff93e85.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161026/selection/d3966fa6dad397334201590e0f540e4a11883bc13a9c1be90588be32d028b895" :answer/id #uuid "1a45165c-c7