 $D.$ Which of the following could be the region $Δ?$" :question/worked-solution "For our transformation $T,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,y=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.\n$$\n\nNotice that if we change $u$ to $r$ and $v$ to $\\theta ,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich represents the usual formulas for changing from polar to Cartesian coordinates. \n\nTherefore, the pre-image $Δ$ of $D$ under the action of $T$ is the region that can be written as \n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{5}}.\n$$\n\nThis is the rectangular region enclosed between\n\n- two vertical lines with Cartesian equations $u=2$ and $u=3,$ and\n\n- two horizontal lines with Cartesian equations $v=0$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{5},$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/968e682dbaa9d8bdb95808e609a1dba6c68e8e12d9cae1abb59755b5ec640286.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-160951/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b327bc4-3944-515e-8b78-f0dbcf55bc74"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160951"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-161116/selection/a08e746ba73a698e8acfd2231d953347c866e99d08e57d691229b7ffae11ec69" :answer/id #uuid "f8725c78-f13c-5f58-aeb8-6c796e9619b1" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047173/assets/89f8cd5fdb19ae5a3eb74bb1d519da855ea6f32027aa3e536c8cea99228c13cb.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161116/selection/61091bce8d5ee73fa76ede9f22dca67043d8578cfb8e7c465fac8c2177e85f28" :answer/id #uuid "60c20a58-d91b-57e2-91fb-660b98740d52" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/m